WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.458
JUSTIN JACKSON:
The dream was never

00:00:01.458 --> 00:00:03.540
one about mastery
or being a lord.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.990
The dream the entire time
was about sustenance,

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.810
about one brother, Joseph,
keeping the others alive.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.690
"And the famine grew
grave in the land.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:18.930
And it happened when they
had eaten up the provisions

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.138
that they had brought to
Egypt that their father said

00:00:21.138 --> 00:00:22.410
to them, 'Go back.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.190
Buy us some food.'

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.950
And Judah said to him saying,
'The man firmly warned us,

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.160
saying 'You shall not see my
face unless your brother is

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.120
with you.'"

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.940
And of course, in verse
11, Israel relents.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.500
He has to relent.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.460
If it must be so, do it.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.010
And of course, they go back.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:43.860
They take double the silver.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:49.830
They bring Benjamin to Joseph,
and they meet Joseph one more

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:50.520
time.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.860
And they explain to him how
they got the silver back

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:57.090
and that they've brought
back even more silver.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.490
And Joseph reassures them,
"'All as well with you.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:00.210
Do not fear.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.920
Your God and the
God of your father

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.569
has placed treasure
for you in your bags.

00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:06.240
Your silver has come to me.'

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.670
And he brought
Simeon out to them.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.740
And the man brought the
men into Joseph's house.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.100
And he gave them water and
they bathe their feet."

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.590
"And they prepared a tribute
against Joseph's arrival

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.410
at noon, for they had heard
that they would eat bread.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.838
And Joseph came into the house.

00:01:20.838 --> 00:01:23.130
And they brought him the
tribute that was in their hand

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.000
into the house.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.850
And they bowed down
to him to the ground."

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:29.020
There's that beautiful
bowing down moment again,

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.460
the dream coming to pass.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.260
"And he asked how they were.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.210
And he said, 'Is
it well with your

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.070
aged father of whom you spoke?

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.510
Is he still alive?'

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:41.420
And they said, 'All is well
with your servant, our father.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:42.920
He is still alive."

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.320
And they bowed
down one more time.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:46.753
"And he raised his eyes."

00:01:46.753 --> 00:01:47.420
And here it is--

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.760
"And he saw Benjamin his
brother, his mother's son.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.208
And he says, 'Is this your
youngest brother of whom you

00:01:53.208 --> 00:01:53.750
spoke to me?'

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.090
And he said, 'God be
gracious to you, my son.'

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.940
And Joseph hurried out, for
his feelings for his brother

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.040
overwhelmed him and
he wanted to weep,

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.830
and he went into the
chamber and wept there.

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:08.509
And he bathed his
face and came out

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:09.979
and he held himself in check.

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:11.450
And he said, 'Serve bread.'"

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.130
And this is a stunning moment.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:16.520
The meal is such a brief
scene, but it's so perfect.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.790
"And they were seated
before him, the firstborn

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.860
according to his
birthright, the youngest

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:25.950
according to his youth, and the
men marveled to each other."

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.010
And of course, what
they're marveling at here

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.990
is that Joseph would
actually know the birth

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:33.470
order, that he can put them
in the correct position.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:35.930
"And he had portions
passed to them from before,

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.510
and Benjamin's portion
was five times more

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.280
than the portion
of all the rest."

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.850
As if Joseph is reminding
them of the favoritism

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:45.710
that is there with Benjamin.

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:47.360
So yes, everything is right.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.460
All the birth orders in place.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:55.460
And yet, we see a favor
heaped upon Benjamin here.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:59.510
And this, of course,
leads us to Chapter 44,

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.360
leads us to Joseph's
ultimate plan

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.360
to put the goblet
inside of Benjamin's bag

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.820
to accuse him of stealing.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:11.630
He says, "How could we steal
from your master's house silver

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:12.380
or gold?

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:16.290
He of your servants with
whom it be found shall die,

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:19.670
and what's more, we shall
become slaves to our Lord.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.120
And he said, 'Even so, as
by your words, let it be--

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.720
he with whom it be found
shall become a slave to me,

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.520
and you shall be clear.'"

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.380
And they hurried and each man
set down his bag on the ground.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.390
And each opened his bag.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:34.340
And he searched,
beginning with the oldest

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.690
and ending with the youngest.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:39.550
And he found the goblet
in Benjamin's bag."

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:42.100
Note what Joseph is
going to do here.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.980
He says, "The man in whose
hand the goblet was found,

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.130
he shall become my
slave, and you, you

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:49.510
go in peace to your father."

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:50.260
Look at that line.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.330
"You go in peace
to your father."

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.490
They know there will
be no peace here

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:56.410
as they go to their father.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.600
And this really is kind
of the stunning moment.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.290
This is Joseph playing off of
the entire history of what they

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:05.020
have done to him, the entire
history of the favoritism

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:05.710
in the family.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.890
Because think about
what they have now.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:13.730
Their father's beloved
son, Benjamin--

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.110
what has he been accused of?

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:16.209
A thief.

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:17.990
Oh, think about
how delicious this

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.240
could be going back to Israel.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.500
They could look at him and say,
your beloved son is a thief.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:29.090
Look at how wrong you
were to favor this thief.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:31.730
But for some reason,
Judah can't do so.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.355
He gives to Joseph
the back story.

00:04:35.355 --> 00:04:36.980
He says, "And your
servant, our father,

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.430
said to us, 'You know that
too did my wife bear me.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:42.440
And one out for
me and I thought,

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:44.220
Oh, he's been torn to shreds.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.250
And I have not seen him since.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:47.900
And should you
take this one, too,

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.360
from my presence
and harm befall him,

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:53.750
you would bring down my gray
head and evil to Sheol.'

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:56.630
And so, should I come to
your servant, my father,

00:04:56.630 --> 00:05:00.440
and the lad not be with
us--" this is so important.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:03.770
"--for his life is
bound to the lad's.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.520
When he saw that the lad was
not with us, he would die.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:09.500
And your servants
would bring down

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:12.470
the gray head of your
servant, our father,

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.780
in sorrow, to Sheol."

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.300
"And so, let your
servant, pray, stay

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:20.330
instead of the lad as
a slave to my Lord,

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:22.430
and let the lad go
up with his brothers.

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.710
For how shall I go
up to my father,

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.780
if the lad not be with us?"

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:31.940
Judah, in this beautiful end to
this penitential narrative, he

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:36.620
who recommended that they
sell Joseph into slavery,

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.930
takes slavery on himself.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:43.310
And he takes slavery on
himself on behalf of one

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:46.340
that he assumes is guilty.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:52.200
And he sacrifices himself
for really a stunning reason.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.860
And that reason is the
love of his father.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:58.970
In many ways, I see Judah
as the hero of this story.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:05:59.930
What would it take?

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:04.760
Think about the love that
he has for his father

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.580
to fear that he would go
down to Sheol mourning.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:13.190
To be able to swallow
all of that rivalry, all

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:15.320
of the enmity that he
has for his brother,

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:17.480
and all of the favoritism
that his father

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:23.220
has been heaping on Joseph
and Benjamin this entire time.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.330
And Judah is willing to
take all that on and stay

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:32.000
in Benjamin's stead out
of love for his father.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.360
And of course, Joseph sees
that the entire narrative

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:38.720
has been disrupted, that
Judah is broken free,

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:40.880
that the Joseph
story is no longer.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.320
That there is
something new here.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:47.490
There is a reconciliation, that
the brothers have come around.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.650
In Chapter 45, we get
to see the reunion.

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:52.920
"And Joseph could no longer hold
himself in check before all who

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:55.050
stood in attendance
upon him, and he cried,

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.940
'Clear out everyone around me.'

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.340
And no man stood with
him when Joseph made

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:00.720
himself known to his brothers.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.940
And he wept aloud, and
the Egyptians heard,

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.290
and the house of Pharaoh heard.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.290
And Joseph said to his
brothers, 'I am Joseph.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.040
Is my father still alive?'

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:11.010
But his brothers
could not answer him,

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:12.900
for they were
dismayed before him.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:16.350
And Joseph said to his brothers,
'Come close to me, pray.'

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.100
And they came
close, and he said,

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:21.120
'I am Joseph, your brother
whom you sold into Egypt.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.820
And so now, do not
be pained and do not

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.370
be incensed with
yourselves that you sold me

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.830
down here, because
for sustenance God

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:31.710
has sent me before you.

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:33.308
Two years now there
has been famine

00:07:33.308 --> 00:07:34.350
in the heart of the land.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.960
And there are yet five years
without plowing and harvest.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:40.410
And God has sent me before you
to make you a remnant on Earth

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:44.220
and to preserve your life for
you to be a great surviving

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.210
group."

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:48.390
And now, to bring this
story of the sibling

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:52.920
rivalry to full circle, Joseph
finally reads his dream.

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:56.850
The dream was never one about
mastery or being a lord.

00:07:56.850 --> 00:08:00.780
The dream the entire time
was about sustenance,

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:04.260
about one brother, Joseph,
keeping the others alive.

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:07.260
He rejects their dream
of lord and master

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:09.990
and rather offers them
this understanding

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:13.380
of this dream, this dream of
sustenance that Joseph will,

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.510
in fact, take care of them.

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:18.360
Joseph the dream
reader now finally

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:21.210
gets to read the dream
of Joseph the dreamer,

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:23.550
the young man who didn't
understand the dreams.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:26.820
He understands now.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:28.170
SPEAKER: Thank you for watching.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:30.140
We hope you're enjoying
our highlight series

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:33.049
and invite you to explore
all of Hillsdale College's

00:08:33.049 --> 00:08:34.250
online courses.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:38.380
They are free and for
everyone who loves to learn.

